7 — Logging & Monitoring (essential)

Log attempts to add non-existent users with IP + timestamp (for abuse detection).

Expose /health for CPU/memory and DB connection status.

Track metrics: contacts added per minute, contact remove rate, rate-limit triggered count.

8 — UX / Client hints (so frontend integrates cleanly)

After login, call GET /contacts before rendering the chat UI.

Keep a local cache of contacts with ETag; update via Socket.IO contact:updated events when contact is changed from other device.

For the “To:” dropdown in the chat composer: show contacts (paginated or cached).

Show presence via presence:update events; animate status changes smoothly.

